{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecoveryTarget_1ppb_remains_conjectural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecoveryTarget_1ppb_remains_conjectural","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L195-L208","doc":"The 1 ppb target itself is **conjectural** — *named*, not asserted (§3b).\nThe conjecture is that the cyclotomic projection at `n_⋆ = 2` produces some\nconcrete `Phi_proj` meeting the 1 ppb recovery target, i.e.\n`∃ phiProj, betaDecayRecoveryTarget phiProj`.  Any future closure must\n(i) compute a specific `Phi_proj` from the projection at `n_⋆ = 2`,\n(ii) show `|Phi_proj - 0.78233341| ≤ 10⁻⁹ · 0.78233341`.  The structural\nlift formula is the open R&D part per `conj:brane-tower-z-habiro`.\n\nThis is the honest replacement for the previous `: True := trivial`\n(vacuous) marker: the `Prop` carries the real existential content; the\n*absence of any proof term* is the honest open state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecovery_at_N0_within_0_2_percent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecovery_at_N0_within_0_2_percent","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L173-L193","doc":"**Concrete witness, conditional.** The single-wrap symbolic\nprediction `Q_β^pred = 0.7836` MeV sits at `+0.168%` relative\nerror vs CODATA — i.e. it satisfies a relaxed recovery target\nat the `2 × 10⁻³` level, which is the *empirical depth-N=0*\nclosure (1.31 keV residual). 1 ppb closure requires the open\nlift formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecoveryTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayRecoveryTarget","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L165-L171","doc":"1 ppb closure target: the cyclotomic projection at `n_⋆ = 2`\nmust produce a `Phi_proj` matching `Q_β^CODATA = 0.78233341` MeV\nto within `1 × 10⁻⁹` relative error. This proposition is\n**conjectural** — the structural lift formula required to\nextract `Phi_proj` is the open part of `brane-tower-z-habiro`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.RecoversWithRelativeError","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.RecoversWithRelativeError","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L128-L148","doc":"Substantive recovery predicate: at level `nStar`, the **caller-\nsupplied** projection value `phiProj` recovers the empirical\nbinding `B_target` to within relative error `eps`.\n\n`phiProj` is an explicit argument (not an `∃`-bound witness) so\nthe predicate has propositional content beyond satisfiability:\na witness must produce a SPECIFIC numerical value derived from\nthe cyclotomic projection `π_{n_⋆}^{(z)}(Φ_q^trans(β))`, not\n\"there exists some real number close to the target.\"\n\n(Per #637 review: the `∃ Phi_proj` form is satisfiable for any\n`B_target, eps > 0` by picking `Phi_proj = B_target`. Taking\n`phiProj` as a concrete input is the strictly-stronger\nrequirement.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayNStarCandidates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.betaDecayNStarCandidates","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L121-L126","doc":"The β-decay sector instance: all three candidates give n_⋆ = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.agreement","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L118-L118","doc":"All three substrate-derived candidates agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.generatorRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.generatorRank","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Generator rank of the Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.coxeterLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.coxeterLength","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Coxeter length of the operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.habiroMMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.habiroMMax","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Habiro m_max from prop:habiro-expansion-atomic (proven). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BraneTowerNStar.NStarCandidates","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BraneTowerNStar.lean#L106-L118","doc":"The level-selection rule `n_⋆` for an operator class is\nderivable from substrate data. The three candidate rules for\nthe β-decay sector all give `n_⋆ = 2`. This structure records\nthe candidates + their agreement check. ","signatureChunk":0}]}